  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s0001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "pam_cifscreds",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "PAM module to manage NTLM credentials in kernel keyring",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "Manual section:",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "8",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "SYNOPSIS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Edit the PAM configuration files for the systems that you want to automatically register NTLM credentials for, e.g. [[p0]]/etc/pam.d/login[[p1]], and modify as follows:",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-open",
            "style": "em"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "style-close",
            "style": "em"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Change DOMAIN to the name of you Windows domain, or use host= as described below.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "DESCRIPTION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The pam_cifscreds PAM module is a tool for automatically adding credentials (username and password) for the purpose of establishing sessions in multiuser mounts.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "When a cifs filesystem is mounted with the \"multiuser\" option, and does not use krb5 authentication, it needs to be able to get the credentials for each user from somewhere. The pam_cifscreds module can be used to provide these credentials to the kernel automatically at login.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "In the session section of the PAM configuration file, the module can either an NT domain name or a list of hostname or addresses.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "OPTIONS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "pam_cifscreds supports a couple options which can be set in the PAM configuration files. You must have one (and only one) of domain= or host=.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "debug",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Turns on some extra debug logging.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0016",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "domain=<NT domain name>",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0017",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Credentials will be added for the specified NT domain name.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0018",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "host=<hostname or IP address>[,...]",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Credentials will be added for the specified hostnames or IP addresses.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "NOTES",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The pam_cifscreds PAM module requires a kernel built with support for the login key type. That key type was added in v3.3 in mainline Linux kernels.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Since pam_cifscreds adds keys to the session keyring, it is highly recommended that one use pam_keyinit to ensure that a session keyring is established at login time.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0023",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "SEE ALSO",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0024",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "cifscreds(1), pam_keyinit(8)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0025",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "AUTHOR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0026",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The pam_cifscreds PAM module was developed by Orion Poplawski <orion@nwra.com>.",
      "protected": []
    }
  ],
